1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:03,120
(Sheldon(on video):)is there any peanut brittle
left in that can?

2
00:00:03,123 --> 00:00:06,293
(Leonard(on video):)You mean this weirdly
suspicious one?

3
00:00:06,292 --> 00:00:08,862
(Sheldon(on video):)Yes. Open it and check.

4
00:00:13,432 --> 00:00:15,662
(Leonard(on video):)I don't get it.

5
00:00:15,668 --> 00:00:18,468
(Leonard(on video):)There's actually
peanut brittle in...

6
00:00:23,876 --> 00:00:25,946
(Leonard(on video):)Please go to Mars.

7
00:00:28,046 --> 00:00:30,046
But on a more serious note:

8
00:00:30,049 --> 00:00:31,619
(Sheldon(on video):)The most important reason I want

9
00:00:31,618 --> 00:00:34,648
(Sheldon(on video):)to go to Mars is that
I believe, as a scientist,

10
00:00:34,654 --> 00:00:37,454
(Sheldon(on video):)it's my duty
to push the boundaries

11
00:00:37,457 --> 00:00:39,887
(Sheldon(on video):)of human knowledge forward.

12
00:00:39,893 --> 00:00:42,623
(Sheldon(on video):)Now, I know that life on Mars
will be difficult.

13
00:00:42,629 --> 00:00:45,729
(Sheldon(on video):)But life here on Earth
is no picnic.

14
00:00:45,732 --> 00:00:48,102
(Sheldon(on video):)Also, picnics are no picnic.

15
00:00:49,601 --> 00:00:51,001
(Sheldon(on video):)Where should we go for lunch?

16
00:00:51,004 --> 00:00:53,174
(Sheldon(on video):)Oh, I know, the ground.

17
00:00:54,339 --> 00:00:55,609
(Sheldon(on video):)In conclusion,

18
00:00:55,608 --> 00:00:57,138
(Sheldon(on video):)thank you for considering me

19
00:00:57,143 --> 00:01:01,023
(Sheldon(on video):)for this journey of a lifetime.

